{
  "name": "hornet",
  "_about": "A hornet -- the European hornet (Vespa crabro), a worker 25 mm long, the largest wasp in Europe: head and thorax chestnut and black, the face and the broad crown behind the eyes yellow-orange; the gaster's first ring chestnut-brown, the second brown edged yellow, the rest yellow with paired brown spots; a pinched waist; red-brown legs and antennae; amber wings folded lengthwise along its sides. Variant: the queen (35 mm). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/hymen.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, elbowed antennae that wave, the wings folded flat over the abdomen -- swung out and beating in the variant \"flying\").",
